---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import PullQuote from '../../components/PullQuote.astro';
import { getGitDates } from '../../lib/git-dates';

// New page, content/faq-and-guides item 2. Brings together, on one
// citable URL, the three pieces of the pouches mechanism that /india/law/
// already covers but spreads across one section among several — the
// FSSAI food-rule bar (Regulation 2.3.4), the DTAB's 27 August 2026
// drug-approval freeze, and the Health Ministry's 19 September 2026 order
// to states. All three facts, and their sourcing, are drawn from
// /india/law/#nicotine-pouches-and-snus and src/data/peca.ts — nothing
// new asserted here. The 19 September order itself isn't quoted directly
// (AVI hasn't seen its full text — see the unreviewed draft statements in
// src/content/press/), only the fact of it and its public reporting.
const pageDates = getGitDates('src/pages/india/nicotine-pouches.astro');

const articleLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Are Nicotine Pouches Legal in India?',
  datePublished: pageDates.published,
  dateModified: pageDates.modified,
  author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Association of Vapers India' },
};
---
<Base
  title="Are Nicotine Pouches Legal in India?"
  description="No law names or bans nicotine pouches in India — but a two-agency regulatory freeze between FSSAI's food rules and CDSCO's drug rules has closed every lawful route to sell them, as of September 2026."
  image="/og/india-law.png"
  wide={true}
>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(articleLd)} />

  <section class="breakout pouch-hero">
    <div class="breakout-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">As of today</p>
      <h1>Are nicotine pouches legal in India?</h1>
      <p class="pouch-hero-sub">Short answer: no law bans them by name — but as of September 2026, there's no lawful way to sell one either. Here's the two-agency freeze that did it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="pouch-body">
    <p class="page-authority">
      By Association of Vapers India · Last reviewed {pageDates.modified}
      <span class="authority-note">· This is AVI's understanding of the regulatory position, not formal legal advice.</span>
    </p>
    <p class="direct-answer">
      <strong>Are nicotine pouches legal in India? No single law says so either way.</strong>
      Nicotine pouches and snus aren't named or banned by any Act of
      Parliament. But two separate regulators have each closed their own
      route to market — together, that adds up to no lawful pathway to
      sell one at all, as of September 2026.
    </p>

    <div class="pouch-timeline">
      <div class="pouch-step">
        <Icon name="document" />
        <h3>No route as a food</h3>
        <p>Nicotine pouches contain no tobacco leaf, so COTPA — the law covering products like khaini and gutka — doesn't apply. That pushes them to the Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI), whose Regulation 2.3.4 bars nicotine as an ingredient in any consumable food product.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pouch-step">
        <Icon name="scale" />
        <h3>No route as a drug — 27 August 2026</h3>
        <p>The other legal home for a purified-nicotine product is as a drug: the Indian Pharmacopoeia lists nicotine as an Active Pharmaceutical Ingredient, so CDSCO treats a new nicotine product as a "new drug" needing clinical trials and therapeutic approval. The Drugs Technical Advisory Board (DTAB) recommended against approving any new nicotine formulations — closing that door too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pouch-step">
        <Icon name="shield" />
        <h3>Enforcement follows — 19 September 2026</h3>
        <p>The Union Health Ministry directed states to act against nicotine-pouch sales, <a href="https://retail.economictimes.indiatimes.com/amp/news/food-entertainment/personal-care-pet-supplies-liquor/india-orders-crackdown-on-nicotine-pouches-citing-health-risks-letter-shows/134496424" target="_blank" rel="noopener">reported by ET Retail</a> days later, citing a letter to states. AVI is reviewing the order's actual text and the states' enforcement directions before taking a litigation position. No Act of Parliament changed — the freeze above is what the enforcement rests on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="split-note">
      This is a regulatory freeze built from two agencies' rules, not a law
      Parliament debated and passed — the same kind of overreach courts
      rejected for e-cigarettes in 2019, when a consumer product was forced
      into "drug" classification despite no manufacturer making a
      therapeutic claim for it. No nicotine pouch is sold in India as a
      cessation aid; they're marketed as consumer products, the same as
      abroad. <a href="/india/law/#nicotine-pouches-and-snus">Full sourcing on /india/law/ →</a>
    </p>

    <h2><Icon name="chart" /> The evidence, set against what stays legal</h2>
    <PullQuote
      quote="Using [nicotine pouches] instead of cigarettes puts you at a lower risk of mouth cancer, heart disease, lung cancer, stroke, emphysema, and chronic bronchitis."
      attribution="US FDA, modified-risk marketing order, June 2026"
    />
    <div class="pouch-compare">
      <div class="pouch-col pouch-fda">
        <p class="split-label">FDA-reviewed, June 2026</p>
        <p>The claim above is the first reduced-risk marketing claim the FDA has ever authorised for a nicotine pouch, after its own scientific review.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pouch-col pouch-slt">
        <p class="split-label">Meanwhile in India</p>
        <p>Loose smokeless tobacco — gutka, khaini — stays legal and openly sold at every paan shop, and is linked to <strong>350,000+</strong> deaths a year, per a peer-reviewed mortality study. A lower-risk pouch stays off the market entirely, while the far more dangerous product doesn't. <a href="/india/smokeless-tobacco/">The full harm reduction case →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2><Icon name="document" /> What this means practically</h2>
    <p>
      This page doesn't sell, advertise or facilitate access to nicotine
      pouches or any other product — AVI's advocacy is aimed at changing
      how this freeze is applied through evidence and engagement with
      regulators, not circumventing it. Brand names, specific
      formulations, prices and sellers are deliberately absent from this
      page and the rest of this site.
    </p>

    <div class="pouch-related">
      <a href="/india/law/#nicotine-pouches-and-snus" class="related-card">
        <h3>The law, in full →</h3>
        <p>Every source behind the FSSAI and DTAB mechanism, plus e-cigarettes and NRT for contrast.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/india/smokeless-tobacco/" class="related-card">
        <h3>India's smokeless tobacco users →</h3>
        <p>The harm reduction case for the roughly 200 million Indians who use gutka, khaini or other SLT.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--gold-light);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }
    .pouch-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(18,19,15,0.85), rgba(18,19,15,0.93)), url('/images/backgrounds/open-sky.jpg');
      background-size: cover;
      background-position: center 60%;
      padding: 3.25rem 0 2.75rem;
    }
    .pouch-hero h1 { color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.85rem; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 2.6rem); }
    .pouch-hero-sub { color: #cdd6cf; font-size: 1.05rem; max-width: 38rem; margin: 0; }

    .pouch-body { max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.75rem 1.5rem 4rem; }
    .page-authority { font-size: 0.82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
    .authority-note { display: block; margin-top: 0.2rem; font-style: italic; }
    @media (min-width: 640px) { .authority-note { display: inline; margin-top: 0; } }
    .direct-answer {
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      background: var(--paper-alt);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      padding: 1.1rem 1.4rem;
      margin: 0 0 2.25rem;
    }

    .pouch-timeline { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; }
    .pouch-step {
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-left: 4px solid var(--gold);
      border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .pouch-step :global(svg) { width: 1.4rem; height: 1.4rem; color: var(--gold-dark); margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    .pouch-step h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.02rem; }
    .pouch-step p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink); }

    .split-note {
      background: var(--paper-alt);
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      margin: 0 0 2.25rem;
    }

    h2 {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 0.6rem;
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    }
    h2 :global(svg) { width: 1.3rem; height: 1.3rem; color: var(--accent); flex-shrink: 0; }

    .pouch-compare {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
    }
    .pouch-col { border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.1rem 1.25rem 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .pouch-col p { font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0; color: var(--ink); }
    .pouch-col .split-label { margin-bottom: 0.6rem; font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.03em; }
    .pouch-fda { background: #eef6f1; border-color: #cfe4d7; }
    .pouch-fda .split-label { color: var(--accent-dark); }
    .pouch-slt { background: #fbf1ec; border-color: #ecd3c4; }
    .pouch-slt .split-label { color: var(--rust-dark); }
    .pouch-slt strong { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.3rem; color: var(--rust-dark); }
    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .pouch-compare { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }

    .pouch-related {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(15rem, 100%), 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin-top: 2.5rem;
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .related-card {
      display: block;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
      background: var(--paper-alt);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease;
    }
    .related-card:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
    .related-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--accent-dark); }
    .related-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  </style>
</Base>
